# Source: https://github.com/lh3/minimap2/issues/738
# Symptom: BED12 record produced by minimap2 splice2bed (paftools.js) where a
#   block has blockSize=0; arises when CIGAR contains two consecutive N (intron-
#   skip) operations separated only by an I (insertion): ...N I N... causes
#   the insertion to be skipped without advancing the position, yielding a
#   zero-length exon block.  Programs that process BED12 blocks reject or crash
#   on blockSize=0 because the spec implies each block has positive length.
chr5	140807067	140884662	read1	0	-	140807067	140884662	0	3	422,0,1242	0,75497,77595
chr5	180549000	180730000	read2	0	+	180549000	180730000	0	3	37,0,500	0,37,180963
